                    correct: 1,
                    explanation: 'Repo rate is the rate at which RBI lends overnight funds to banks. When it rises, banks\' own cost of funds rises, which they transmit to loans (home loans, car loans, business loans) through MCLR. A 0.5% repo rate hike typically translates to 0.4-0.5% rise in bank lending rates within 2-3 months. On ₹50L home loan, this means approximately ₹1,500-₹1,800 higher EMI per month.',
