                    q: 'When the RBI cuts the repo rate, the expected effect on equity markets is:',
                    options: ['Markets always fall — lower rates signal economic weakness', 'Markets often rise — lower rates reduce corporate borrowing costs, increase future profit expectations, and make equity more attractive relative to fixed income', 'No effect — stock markets only respond to company earnings', 'Markets always rise by exactly the rate cut percentage'],
                    correct: 1,
